      {
        "id": 191866,
        "name": "robb8888",
        "username": "robb8888",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-03-28T02:13:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mwc146\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n mwc146:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm tellin' ya, OX makes Cosmitron&nbsp;<em>much</em> more manageable. With a decent opening draw, you never have to see his flip side.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Interesting how philosophies differ – with the crew I used (Legacy, TLT, Parse, DV, Bunker), I much prefer Cosmi-tron flipped. &nbsp;On his regular side, he plays two cards, and it's harder to use Parse/DV effectively to control him. &nbsp;On his reverse side, I used Legacy to tank his energy damage, and between Parse, DV, and Bunker's Foam Grenades, it was easy to keep both the environment and Cosmi's deck in check to prevent surprises. &nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 82,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:18:31.370Z",
